=== Prompt ===
Who is Queen Elizabeth II?

=== Response ===
Queen Elizabeth II is the current and longest-reigning monarch of the United Kingdom and the other Commonwealth realms. She ascended the throne on February 6, 1952, at the age of 25, and has reigned for more than 69 years as of 2023.

Born on April 21, 1926, Elizabeth was the first child of King George VI and Queen Elizabeth (later the Queen Mother). She was educated privately and at the royal residence, and during World War II, she undertook duties that included nursing, driving an ambulance, and delivering messages to the military.

Elizabeth married Philip Mountbatten, Duke of Edinburgh, in 1947, and they have four children: Charles, Prince of Wales; Anne, Princess Royal; Andrew, Duke of York; and Edward, Earl of Wessex.

Elizabeth II has been the symbol of the British monarchy and has played a significant role in the political, social, and cultural history of the United Kingdom and the Commonwealth. She has traveled extensively, undertaking official visits to more than 130 countries during her reign.

Elizabeth II is also known for her commitment to public service, charitable work, and the promotion of the arts and education. She has received numerous honors and awards, including the George Cross, the Order of Merit, and the Order of the Garter.

In 2015, Elizabeth II became the longest-reigning British monarch, surpassing her great-great-grandmother Queen Victoria. She is also the oldest and longest-serving current monarch in the world. Elizabeth II's son, Prince Charles, is the heir apparent to the throne.

